cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "USearch: One Proximity Graph for Search, Sparse Products and Attention, across RAM, VRAM and NVMe"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/USearch
url: https://github.com/unum-cloud/USearch
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7949415
abstract: >-
  USearch is an open-source proximity-graph index for nearest-neighbor search over dense vectors,
  sequences, shapes and geospatial sets. The same graph serves as a sparse operand, folding sparse
  matrix products, late-interaction MaxSim scoring and softmax attention into its traversal, and one
  checkpoint opens in host memory, GPU memory or on NVMe drives without being rewritten. Its core
  is a header-only C++ 20 library with no external dependencies, and ClickHouse, DuckDB, ScyllaDB
  and YugabyteDB embed it for vector search.
keywords:
  - nearest-neighbor search
  - vector search
  - similarity search
  - proximity graph
  - sparse matrix multiplication
  - attention
  - nvme
  - gpu

